<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/ef2a6d1e-41e1-4276-ab10-9789bcecfd8c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-12T02:25:07.241488Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/ef2a6d1e-41e1-4276-ab10-9789bcecfd8c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Detect a plain cl.exe in build.rs (Tool::is_like_msvc && !is_like_clang_cl) and switch with build.compiler(\"clang-cl\"): more code than cc's built-in option and it would override an explicit CC." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97328bf2-f1f3-49e8-bf79-3a773ae81f18> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97328bf2-f1f3-49e8-bf79-3a773ae81f18> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "clang-cl for MSVC builds of vendored SLOP C" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97328bf2-f1f3-49e8-bf79-3a773ae81f18> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97328bf2-f1f3-49e8-bf79-3a773ae81f18> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Both -sys build scripts call cc::Build::prefer_clang_cl_over_msvc(true), and slop-std-sys links pthread only when CARGO_CFG_TARGET_OS != \"windows\". Windows support arrived with SLOP 0.4.1 (slop-lang/slop #327/#328/#329): slop_runtime.h threads through pthreads on POSIX and _beginthreadex/SRW locks/condition variables/InitOnce on Win32, and std io/strlib use the MS CRT with 64-bit offsets. The generated C uses GNU statement expressions (~230 sites) and __auto_type (~1000 sites), which MSVC's cl.exe rejects. cc-rs uses cl.exe by default on *-windows-msvc, and upstream SLOP documents and CI-tests clang-cl and MinGW-w64 gcc as the supported Windows compilers. prefer_clang_cl_over_msvc changes only cc-rs's default for MSVC targets: CC/CC_<target> still override it, and it is a no-op elsewhere. It needs cc >= 1.2.35, so the build-dependency is cc = \"1.2.35\"; MSRV resolution still selects cc 1.4.0, which has it. CI covers windows-latest on MSVC (in the stable matrix) and x86_64-pc-windows-gnu with MSYS2 MINGW64 gcc. Applied in slop-std-sys 0.4.2 / slop-rdf-sys 0.5.1 (branch slop-0.4.2)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97328bf2-f1f3-49e8-bf79-3a773ae81f18> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97328bf2-f1f3-49e8-bf79-3a773ae81f18> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-12T02:25:07.241488Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
