<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "slop-rdf was tagged v0.4.0 at the vendored commit c14fe19. The repo convention (commit 7d218ee) is that each -sys crate version matches its upstream library version, so slop-rdf-sys became 0.4.0 instead of a patch bump, and the slop-rdf-commit pin was dropped in favor of the tag." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T06:47:44.976199Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1b00fd84-62df-4a1c-9307-a2410e3f410f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1b00fd84-62df-4a1c-9307-a2410e3f410f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1b00fd84-62df-4a1c-9307-a2410e3f410f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1b00fd84-62df-4a1c-9307-a2410e3f410f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1b00fd84-62df-4a1c-9307-a2410e3f410f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Applied for SLOP 0.4.2 + slop-rdf 0.5.1, which bring Windows support. Changes from the previous procedure: (a) the post-process also rewrites `#include <slop_runtime.h>`, which slop_thread.h has had since 0.4.0 and slop_file.h since 0.4.2, and verification now includes a downstream-include check; see the Lesson \"Generated SLOP headers include the runtime with angle brackets too\". (b) The versioning rule now covers re-vendoring an unchanged upstream: when a SLOP upgrade changes a published -sys crate's C but slop-rdf has no new release, tag slop-rdf with a patch version at the same commit (v0.5.1 = v0.5.0's commit 14bf0d6) so the crate version still matches upstream. (c) The link tests exercise file and thread code, not only symbol presence, so the Windows CI legs run the Win32 paths." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1b00fd84-62df-4a1c-9307-a2410e3f410f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1b00fd84-62df-4a1c-9307-a2410e3f410f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-12T02:25:36.761789Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1b00fd84-62df-4a1c-9307-a2410e3f410f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Applied again for SLOP 0.4.0 + slop-rdf 0.5.0. The procedure is refined with exact source paths, the type-check step (`slop check` needs a single file, so `slop build` is the project-level check), the native-toolchain dependency on the ~/code/slop checkout, and a full-archive link verification. The link tests alone only pull in a few objects." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-06T02:30:40.067617Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
